<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Weekly haftarot, keyed by parsha (`n` on `week`).

  A reading is a custom with one or more `span` children. `from` and `to` are
  `chapter:verse` (or `chapter`, which starts at verse 1). Omit `to` for a
  single verse. `book` may be set on week, custom or span; a descendant
  supplies it if the ancestor does not. from/to are never inherited.

  `n` on custom is a custom name or a comma-separated list of names. A custom
  with no entry follows its parent (see Custom.xml). `Common` is the root;
  write it explicitly when it has a reading.

  `reads="inherit"`: this custom has no reading of its own; the element
  carries sources/comment only. `reads="none"`: this custom reads nothing
  (omission would inherit). Nested `variant`: a reading recorded beside the
  custom's own, never resolved to. `n` on variant narrows it to a subset of
  the parent custom's names.

  `sources` names works from ReadingSources.xml (comma-separated).
  `comment` is what the sources do not settle.
  `precedenceWhenCombined`: customs for which this parsha's haftarah wins
  when combined with the next.
-->
